  "task": "Completeness review of the Larchmont Benefit Services submission received 2026-06-19. Check the consumer notice against the checklist, reconcile the resident figures, confirm which data elements were involved and recommend an outcome."
 },
 "ma_checklist": {
  "personal_information_definition": "A resident's first name or first initial and last name in combination with any of: (a) Social Security number; (b) driver's license or state-issued ID card number; (c) financial account number or credit or debit card number. Addresses, dates of birth and plan elections are not personal information on their own.",
  "consumer_notice_must_include": [
   "The resident's right to obtain a police report",
   "How to request a security freeze, the information needed to request one, and that there is no charge",
   "Details of complimentary credit monitoring, which must be offered for at least 18 months when Social Security numbers were involved",
   "The name of the parent or affiliated corporation if the notifying entity is a subsidiary"
  ],
  "consumer_notice_must_not_include": [
   "The nature of the breach or unauthorized acquisition or use",
   "The number of Massachusetts residents affected"
  ],
  "regulator_form_must_include": "Nature of the breach, number of Massachusetts residents affected, steps taken, whether the organization maintains a written information security program (WISP)."
 },
 "regulator_form": {
  "organization": "Larchmont Benefit Services, LLC",
  "parent_or_affiliate": "Corbel Health Holdings, Inc.",
  "date_breach_discovered": "05/21/2026",
  "breach_type": "Electronic - hacking",
  "nature_of_breach": "Unauthorized access to a secure file-transfer (SFTP) server used by client employers to upload benefits files; files copied on 05/19/2026 and 05/20/2026.",
  "ma_residents_affected": "1,284",
  "personal_information_involved": "Social Security number; financial account number",
  "maintains_wisp": "Yes",
  "credit_monitoring_offered": "Yes - 24 months",
  "consumer_notices_mailed": "06/18/2026",
  "steps_taken": "Took server sftp-ingest-02 offline; reset SFTP credentials for all client accounts as a precaution; added IP allow-listing; engaged Northpoint Forensics; reported the incident to the FBI Boston field office on 05/23/2026."
 },
 "consumer_notice_sample": "[Larchmont Benefit Services letterhead]\nJune 18, 2026\n\nDear <<First Name>> <<Last Name>>,\n\nWe are writing to let you know about a data security incident that may have involved some of your personal information. Larchmont Benefit Services administers benefits enrollment for your employer. On May 21, 2026, we learned that an unauthorized party had accessed a secure file-transfer server that employers use to send us enrollment and payroll-deduction files, and had copied some of those files on May 19 and 20, 2026.\n\nThe information involved may include your name and <<Variable: Social Security number / bank account and routing number / date of birth and home address>>.\n\nTo help protect you, we are offering a complimentary 24-month membership in CredSentry Plus credit monitoring and identity restoration. To enroll, visit www.credsentry-enroll.example or call 1-877-555-0136 and use the code printed below. You must enroll by September 30, 2026.\n\nYou have the right to obtain a police report regarding this incident. If you are the victim of identity theft, you also have the right to file a police report and obtain a copy of it.\n\nMassachusetts law allows you to place a security freeze on your credit reports at no charge. To request a freeze, contact each of the three nationwide consumer reporting agencies online, by phone or by mail. You may need to provide your full name, address, date of birth, Social Security number, proof of current address and a copy of a government-issued ID.\n\nIf you have questions, call 1-877-555-0136, Monday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 8 p.m. Eastern.\n\nSincerely,\nGraham Okonjo-Reyes, President\n\nLarchmont Benefit Services, LLC is a subsidiary of Corbel Health Holdings, Inc.\nEnrollment code: <<Code>>",
 "forensic_summary": {
  "firm": "Northpoint Forensics",
  "date": "2026-06-12",
  "findings": [
   "Server sftp-ingest-02 logs show an unauthorized session from 05/19/2026 22:41 UTC to 05/20/2026 03:17 UTC.",
   "During that session, the folders /inbound/C091_census, /inbound/C114_enroll and /inbound/C207_hsa_deduct were listed and their files downloaded (2.1 GB in total).",
   "No access to /inbound/C162_enroll or /inbound/C233_cobra was found in the logs.",
   "No evidence of access to Larchmont's enrollment database or to any other server.",
   "Log retention on sftp-ingest-02 is 180 days; full logs were preserved."
  ]
 },
 "data_inventory_excerpt": [
  {
   "folder": "/inbound/C091_census",
   "contents": "Annual benefits census: employee name, date of birth, home address, plan elections. No SSNs; the client uses Larchmont member IDs."
  },
  {
   "folder": "/inbound/C114_enroll",
   "contents": "Enrollment files: employee and dependent names, SSNs, dates of birth, plan elections."
  },
  {
   "folder": "/inbound/C162_enroll",
   "contents": "Enrollment files: employee names, SSNs, dates of birth."
  },
  {
   "folder": "/inbound/C207_hsa_deduct",
   "contents": "HSA payroll-deduction files: employee names, employee IDs, contribution amounts, bank account and routing numbers used to fund HSAs."
  },
  {
   "folder": "/inbound/C233_cobra",
   "contents": "COBRA notice files: names, home addresses, qualifying event dates."
  }
 ],
 "client_register": [
  {
   "code": "C091",
   "client": "Wexmoor Regional School District",
   "state": "MA"
  },
  {
   "code": "C114",
   "client": "Brantwood Precision Optics, Inc.",
   "state": "MA / NH"
  },
  {
   "code": "C162",
   "client": "Saltmarsh Brewing Co.",
   "state": "MA"
  },
  {
   "code": "C207",
   "client": "Halvorsen Marine Supply, LLC",
   "state": "MA / RI"
  },
  {
   "code": "C233",
   "client": "Pell & Tierney Architects",
   "state": "CT"
  }
 ],
 "ma_resident_counts": {
  "prepared_by": "Larchmont data team, 2026-06-15",
  "rows": [
   {
    "folder": "/inbound/C091_census",
    "ma_residents": 310,
    "note": "Notified voluntarily"
   },
   {
    "folder": "/inbound/C114_enroll",
    "ma_residents": 702,
    "note": "Includes dependents"
   },
   {
    "folder": "/inbound/C207_hsa_deduct",
    "ma_residents": 236,
    "note": ""
   }
  ]
 },
 "call_center_faq": "Q: Is this letter real? A: Yes. Larchmont Benefit Services mailed these letters on June 18, 2026. We will never ask for your full Social Security number by phone. Q: Why did Larchmont have my information? A: Your employer uses Larchmont to run benefits enrollment and payroll deductions. Q: Was my health information involved? A: Plan elections may show which plan you chose, but no claims or medical records were stored on the affected server. Q: My letter mentions my bank account. What should I do? A: Contact your bank, ask about monitoring or changing the account, and watch your HSA contributions. Q: Can I enroll after September 30? A: No; please enroll before the deadline. Q: I got two letters. A: You may have been enrolled through two employers, or as both an employee and a dependent.",
 "mail_house_email": "From: Dana Whitcombe, Ironbridge Mail Services. To: Larchmont privacy team. Date: June 19, 2026. All 9,870 letters (all states) were dropped at the Brockton facility yesterday, first-class presort. NCOA address updates were applied to 412 records. Postage invoice to follow ($5,183.40). We expect a 2-3% return rate; returned envelopes will be scanned and listed weekly. Spanish versions went to the 64 Halvorsen employees flagged in your file.",
 "prior_submissions_note": "Larchmont filed one earlier Massachusetts notice, in 2023: a misdirected mailing of COBRA notices affecting 14 residents. That file was closed without action.",
 "counsel_cover_letter": "From: Hollis & Varga LLP. Date: June 19, 2026. To: Office of the Attorney General and Office of Consumer Affairs and Business Regulation. We represent Larchmont Benefit Services, LLC ('Larchmont') of Quincy, Massachusetts, a third-party administrator of employee benefits and a subsidiary of Corbel Health Holdings, Inc. We write on Larchmont's behalf to report a data security incident. Larchmont notified 1,284 Massachusetts residents by first-class mail on June 18, 2026 and is offering them complimentary credit monitoring and identity restoration for 24 months. Larchmont maintains a written information security program and is reviewing it in light of this incident. A sample consumer notice is enclosed. Larchmont has also notified the attorneys general of New Hampshire and Rhode Island. Please direct any questions to the undersigned.",
 "wisp_excerpt": "Section 7.3 (File transfer): Client files must be deleted from inbound folders within 30 days after successful import. Section 7.4: SFTP client accounts use key-based authentication or passwords of at least 16 characters; administrative access requires multi-factor authentication. Section 9.1: Suspected security incidents are escalated to the Privacy Officer within 24 hours. Section 11.2: The program is reviewed at least annually and after any incident involving personal information.",
 "client_hr_email": "From: HR Benefits, Brantwood Precision Optics. Date: June 22, 2026. Several employees asked whether their dependents' information was involved and why their children received separate letters. Can you confirm how letters for minor dependents were addressed? -- Reply from Larchmont privacy team, June 22: Yes, dependents were included. Letters for dependents under 18 were addressed to the parent or guardian at the employee's home address, and each dependent received a separate enrollment code."
}

